                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Everything feels toned down from the first game, spells are much less chaotic and just really lackluster overall, you're supposed use the element that the enemy is weak against, spamming the same shit over and over again until they are dead. Sure, in the first game you could also just create one OP spell combo and instakill everything, but experimenting and coming up with said spell combo was really fun.\r\n\r\nNo fun spells like Crash To Desktop from the first game (or Summon Death). The campaign was insanely short, less than 5 hours in total. Only has laughable 3 DLC to buy, which only one includes actual new gameplay.",
